<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<Description>Norse forward-only tabular ingestion: a canonical ITabularReader contract over Sep (delimited) and Sylvan.Data.Excel (single-sheet Excel), for turning untrusted source files into cell spans. Scalar-value conversion of those spans into typed values is Norse.Primitives' job, composed by the caller — this project carries no dependency on it. Native AOT: Sep is fully AOT-clean. ExcelTabularReader/Sylvan.Data.Excel publish under Native AOT with one documented, suppressed trim-analysis finding (IL2093 - see the InternalsVisibleTo item group comment below), inherent to Sylvan.Data.Excel 0.5.6 itself and not this project's own code, pending an upstream fix.</Description>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<!-- SepTabularReader/ExcelTabularReader are internal sealed per the tabular-ingestion design (reachable only
		     through ITabularReader) - $(AssemblyName).Tests already has the sanctioned door via src/Directory.Build.props.
		     The AOT smoke test (Task 3) is a second, concrete, justified caller that constructs them directly to prove
		     Native AOT compatibility; it gets its own narrow door rather than widening the shared one.

		     That smoke test's Native AOT publish carries a documented, suppressed trim-analysis finding: IL2093 on
		     Sylvan.Data.Excel.ExcelDataReader.GetFieldType - an annotation mismatch between Sylvan's override and the
		     DbDataReader.GetFieldType base declaration it overrides, inherent to Sylvan.Data.Excel 0.5.6 itself and
		     unavoidable by any consumer of ExcelDataReader (the type ExcelTabularReader wraps) under AOT trim
		     analysis; ExcelTabularReader never calls GetFieldType directly. Same class of justified suppression as
		     the CA1036/CA2225 SuppressMessage attributes on SequentialGuid/DeterministicGuid: the analyzer's default
		     posture conflicts with a deliberate design fact, so it gets a narrow, cited suppression rather than
		     silence. The suppression itself (`<NoWarn>IL2093</NoWarn>`) lives on the AOT-published exe project
		     (tests/smoke/Primitives.Ingestion.Aot.Smoke.csproj) because $(NoWarn) is evaluated per-project and ILC
		     only runs there - it does not flow across this ProjectReference boundary. Any future downstream Native
		     AOT consumer of ExcelTabularReader needs the same `<NoWarn>IL2093</NoWarn>` until this ships as a NuGet
		     package with buildTransitive props (deferred, per src/Primitives.Ingestion's packaging ledger) or Sylvan
		     fixes the annotation mismatch upstream. -->
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="Norse.Primitives.Ingestion.Aot.Smoke" />
		<PackageReference Include="Sep" Version="*" />
		<PackageReference Include="Sylvan.Data.Excel" Version="*" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
